# CLI Coding Conventions

## stdout vs stderr — CRITICAL

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — breaks JSON IPC frames
console.log('done');

// ✅ GOOD — goes to stderr, safe in daemon mode
import { toddspectLog } from '../log.js';
toddspectLog('done');
```

`toddspectLog()` routes to stderr when `TODDSPECT_IPC=1`, stdout otherwise.

## IPC Frame Writing

```typescript
// Always use writeFrame() — never write to stdout directly
writeFrame({ id: msg.id, action: 'chat:chunk', payload: { ... } });
```

## Error Handling in Connectors

Connectors must call `onError(string)` and never throw to the router:

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
throw new Error('API failed');

// ✅ GOOD
req.onError(`Copilot request failed: ${err.message}`);
return;
```

## Import Paths

All CLI imports use `.js` extension (ESM):

```typescript
import { loadToddSpectConfig } from '../config.js';   // ✅
import { loadToddSpectConfig } from '../config';       // ❌
```

## Config Access

Always use `loadToddSpectConfig(specsDir?)` — never read env vars or files directly:

```typescript
const config = loadToddSpectConfig(specsDir);
const token = config.connectors.copilot.token;
```

## Copilot Auth

`gho_` tokens need exchange via `getCopilotApiToken()` before calling `api.githubcopilot.com`.
Fallback: use token directly when exchange returns 404 (Business/Enterprise accounts).
